WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:15.864
a show shirt?"

2
00:00:16.244 --> 00:00:16.964
Cole asked.

3
00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:23.386
"It's a special kind of shirt that you wear under your show coat," Daisy said with a frown.

4
00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:27.447
"Mine was hanging by my pony's stall earlier.

5
00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:32.068
But when I went back there just now to get changed, it was gone!"

6
00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:35.054
"Is your show coat missing too?"

7
00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.055
Henry asked.

8
00:00:36.075 --> 00:00:39.498
"No, it's just her shirt," Maggie said.

9
00:00:39.518 --> 00:00:42.440
"Don't worry, Daisy," she went on.

10
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.783
"The Lemonade Detectives are on the case!"

11
00:00:45.803 --> 00:00:49.226
"Thanks." Daisy still looked worried.

12
00:00:49.246 --> 00:00:54.071
"I really hope you can solve the mystery before my first class.

13
00:00:55.092 --> 00:00:57.894
I'll never win a blue ribbon if I'm wearing this!"

14
00:00:58.335 --> 00:00:59.656
She pointed to her T-shirt.

15
00:01:01.068 --> 00:01:04.891
"Ms. Wood said fancy clothes aren't mandatory," Maggie reminded her.

16
00:01:04.911 --> 00:01:07.153
"You just told me that."

17
00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.175
"I know," Daisy said.

18
00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:12.417
But she still looked worried.

19
00:01:13.478 --> 00:01:14.839
"What does your shirt look like?"

20
00:01:15.139 --> 00:01:15.900
Henry asked.

21
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.625
"It's mostly white, with long sleeves and a high collar," Daisy said.

22
00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:28.390
"There's a pocket in the front with a strip of pink and yellow polka-dotted ribbon across the top."

23
00:01:29.531 --> 00:01:30.432
Henry looked around.

24
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:34.974
A lot of the other riders were wearing long-sleeved white shirts with high collars.

25
00:01:35.914 --> 00:01:37.495
But none of them had pockets like that.

26
00:01:37.515 --> 00:01:41.837
"It sounds like your shirt will be easy to spot," he told Daisy.

27
00:01:41.857 --> 00:01:44.118
"We'll see what we can do."

28
00:01:44.138 --> 00:01:47.339
"Thanks." Daisy sounded distracted.

29
00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:53.782
"I'd better go see if anyone has an extra shirt I can borrow, just in case."

30
00:01:53.802 --> 00:01:56.983
"Are you guys crazy?"

31
00:01:57.243 --> 00:01:58.724
Cole said after Daisy left.

32
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.741
"We don't have time to solve a mystery today.

33
00:02:02.581 --> 00:02:04.602
We're supposed to be selling lemonade!"

34
00:02:04.622 --> 00:02:06.642
"We can do both."

35
00:02:06.882 --> 00:02:08.003
Maggie sounded excited.

36
00:02:08.023 --> 00:02:13.464
"If we solve the case quickly, maybe I can use the detective fee to enter more classes!"

37
00:02:14.545 --> 00:02:16.405
Cole frowned but didn't say anything else.

38
00:02:17.486 --> 00:02:20.146
Henry wondered if he was thinking about swim team practice.

39
00:02:21.327 --> 00:02:24.748
Cole loved being on the swim team, and he hated to miss a practice.

40
00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:29.375
If they finished early at the show, Cole might have time to get to the pool for part

41
00:02:29.395 --> 00:02:30.256
of today's practice.

42
00:02:31.257 --> 00:02:34.540
But that probably wouldn't happen if they were busy trying to solve a mystery.

43
00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.962
"I agree with Maggie," Henry told Cole.

44
00:02:37.983 --> 00:02:40.905
"I think we should try to solve the case.

45
00:02:41.806 --> 00:02:43.427
Daisy seems really upset."

46
00:02:43.447 --> 00:02:47.130
"Good, then let's get started," Maggie said.

47
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:51.874
"Why don't we—" She stopped talking when Ms.

48
00:02:51.914 --> 00:02:53.576
Wood hurried up to the lemonade stand.

49
00:02:54.504 --> 00:02:56.886
"There you are, Maggie," the stable owner said.

50
00:02:56.906 --> 00:03:00.808
"It's time to get Big Spot ready for your first class."

51
00:03:00.828 --> 00:03:02.469
"Oh, right."

52
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:03.971
Maggie slapped her forehead.

53
00:03:03.991 --> 00:03:06.012
"Sorry, Ms.

54
00:03:06.072 --> 00:03:07.553
Wood. I got distracted."

55
00:03:09.134 --> 00:03:10.375
She started to follow Ms.

56
00:03:10.435 --> 00:03:11.295
Wood toward the barn.

57
00:03:13.337 --> 00:03:18.320
Then she rushed back to the lemonade stand and whispered, "You guys should start investigating!"

58
00:03:19.481 --> 00:03:21.402
Henry nodded as Maggie hurried off again.

59
00:03:21.422 --> 00:03:23.824
"Okay," he said to Cole.

60
00:03:24.412 --> 00:03:27.175
"We should start by checking out the scene of the crime.

61
00:03:28.336 --> 00:03:30.197
Maybe the thief left some clues."

62
00:03:31.198 --> 00:03:32.359
Cole glanced past him.

63
00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:35.081
"Here come some more customers," he said.

64
00:03:35.101 --> 00:03:38.424
"Why don't you serve them while I go look for clues in the barn?"

65
00:03:39.445 --> 00:03:42.388
Henry was surprised that Cole was volunteering to look for clues.

66
00:03:43.469 --> 00:03:45.590
Cole hadn't seemed very interested in the case.

67
00:03:46.551 --> 00:03:49.294
But Cole rushed off before Henry could say anything about that.

68
00:03:49.314 --> 00:03:51.876
"One lemonade, please!"

69
00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.654
a little boy cried, tossing a quarter on the table.

70
00:03:54.674 --> 00:03:58.496
"You got it," Henry said, reaching for the nearest pitcher.

71
00:03:59.457 --> 00:04:02.138
For the next few minutes, he was too busy to think about the case.

72
00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:06.321
Finally the latest group of lemonade customers had all been served.

73
00:04:07.641 --> 00:04:08.982
Henry looked over toward the barn.

74
00:04:09.783 --> 00:04:12.404
Henry guessed that Cole was still inside looking for clues.

75
00:04:13.505 --> 00:04:14.826
He thought about going to help him.

76
00:04:15.746 --> 00:04:18.068
But he wasn't sure he should leave the lemonade stand.

77
00:04:20.064 --> 00:04:22.725
Then he spotted Daisy walking past, leading a pony.

78
00:04:23.706 --> 00:04:26.967
The pony was a little taller than Maggie's favorite pony, Big Spot.

79
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.969
It had a glossy brown coat and a black mane and tail.

80
00:04:31.989 --> 00:04:35.190
Daisy led the pony into the shade of some tall trees nearby.

81
00:04:37.011 --> 00:04:40.192
She leaned against one of the trees, and the pony began to graze.

82
00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:44.894
Henry looked around to make sure no more lemonade customers were coming.

83
00:04:45.895 --> 00:04:48.436
Then he left the lemonade stand and hurried over to Daisy.

84
00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.901
"Hi," he said.

85
00:04:50.921 --> 00:04:52.562
"What are you doing?"

86
00:04:52.582 --> 00:04:58.106
"Coco likes to roll in her stall," Daisy said, gesturing toward the grazing pony.

87
00:04:58.126 --> 00:05:03.030
"I'm trying to keep her moving so she doesn't get dirty before our classes.

88
00:05:04.311 --> 00:05:06.012
Did you find my show shirt yet?"

89
00:05:06.032 --> 00:05:08.955
"We're working on it," Henry said.

90
00:05:09.915 --> 00:05:12.718
He opened his mouth to ask her more questions about her show shirt.

91
00:05:13.738 --> 00:05:15.700
But then he noticed someone rushing toward them.

92
00:05:16.776 --> 00:05:19.620
It was a girl around Daisy's age with a long blond braid.

93
00:05:20.481 --> 00:05:21.342
She looked angry.

94
00:05:21.362 --> 00:05:26.228
"Hey!" the girl yelled, ignoring Henry and pointing a finger at Daisy.

95
00:05:26.248 --> 00:05:28.351
"You stole my pony!"
